{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["And a knob under the two branches, of it — those coming out of it, from the middle branch, which is the main body of the lampstand." "For the six branches — three times 'and a knob (and blossoms)' was not needed to write 'for the six branches' as is written in the first verse, for it counts all of them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The lemma in parentheses (וכפות) 'and blossoms' is supplied by the editor from the biblical text; the logic is that Scripture already tallied all six branches in the first verse, so repeating the distributive phrase for each set of two is unnecessary."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:06.108113189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}